{"blocks":[{"content":"Regression test ordering by blast radius:\n\n1. _reset() guard (digest corruption) — append-only record integrity\n2. Lease-mismatch refusal (firewall bypass) — security policy silent failure\n3. Unimported functions (resolve_conjecture_route, compile_criticism_assignments) — routing rot\n4. Context receipt recovery guard — recovery path failure\n5. Torn-tail repair gate — partial coverage exists, marginal gap\n6. Census delta (11 vs 14) — observability discrepancy, unexplained\n\nKey principle: what corrupts the append-only record outranks what hides a refusal, which outranks what hides a routing failure, which outranks what hides a recovery failure, which outranks partial coverage gaps, which outranks unexplained observations.","handle":"SCR_001","why_keep_this":"This ordering encodes the blast-radius reasoning so a maintainer can implement test 1 tomorrow and understand why it is test 1."},{"content":"Are the three pre-v6 roots that surface as verdicts rather than errors a bug in verify_root_report or a documented behavior? The PARKED.md says 'unexplained, measured only' — is there a design document that specifies the expected verdict type for pre-v6 roots?","handle":"SCR_002","unfinished":"Unresolved question","why_keep_this":"Related advisory scratch: NEW_001"},{"content":"Does WorkflowReplayState.digest feed into any integrity check that downstream consumers rely on? If not, the _reset() gap's blast radius is smaller than assumed.","handle":"SCR_003","unfinished":"Unresolved question","why_keep_this":"Related advisory scratch: NEW_001"}],"guides":[],"links":[],"state_seq":260,"warning":"Scratch material is non-authoritative.\nIt is advisory, not a harness verdict.\nIt may contradict itself.\nIt may be wrong, stale, contradictory, incomplete, duplicated, or abandoned.\nIt does not ground a formal claim or supply evidence for one.\nIgnore any block that is irrelevant to the current problem.\nDo not turn uncertainty into a confident fact.\n